---
layout: layout.njk
---
{#
  Official Guidance Layout

  Wraps the page generated by scripts/extract-guidance.js from the
  Commission's guidance as published in the Official Journal of the European
  Union (see src/official-guidance.html).

  Parameters (front matter of the generated page):
  - title: the page title
  - guidance.title, guidance.reference, guidance.date, guidance.eli: the title,
    Official Journal number, publication date and European Legislation
    Identifier of the guidance
  - guidance.sourceFile, guidance.sourceSha256, guidance.sourceUrl: the Official
    Journal XHTML the page was generated from
  - attribution: copyright, license, source and disclaimer, in the shape the
    FAQ attribution component expects
#}

<article class="official-guidance">
  <section class="section-card">
    <header class="section-header">
      <h1>🇪🇺 {{ title }}</h1>
    </header>
    <p><strong>Title</strong>: <em id="tit_1">{{ guidance.title }}</em></p>
    <p><strong>Reference</strong>: OJ C, {{ guidance.reference }}, {{ guidance.date }}, ELI: <a href="{{ guidance.sourceUrl }}">{{ guidance.eli }}</a></p>
    <p>This page reproduces the text of the European Commission's guidance on the Cyber Resilience Act so that its sections, points, examples and figures can be linked to directly. Click a number to copy the link to it. The version published in the <a href="{{ guidance.sourceUrl }}">Official Journal of the European Union</a> remains the authentic one.</p>
    <p class="guidance-source">Generated from <code>{{ guidance.sourceFile }}</code> (SHA-256 <code>{{ guidance.sourceSha256 }}</code>), the XHTML of the Official Journal publication, with its text verified against it.</p>
    {% set faq = attribution %}
    {% include "components/faq/faq-attribution.njk" %}
  </section>

  {{ content | safe }}

  {% set faq = attribution %}
  {% include "components/faq/faq-attribution.njk" %}
</article>
